          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto",
          "value": "\n<ol dir=\"ltr\"><li>May God prolong the life of my brother and dear master, and shield you, protect you, watch over you, guard you, and make your benefactions eternal.</li>\n<li>I am writing to you on the eve of the Fast of Kippur, may God accept it from us, from you, and from all Isr(ael) with forgiveness and good pleasure,</li>\n<li>in well-being, health and well-ordered circumstances, according to the best of the Creator&rsquo;s customary favors, may He be exalted and glorified, and the greatest of His benefits,</li>\n<li>we and the rest of our community, abundant praise be to Him. Likewise, your son \u1e62adaqa, may God keep him, and the household, and all</li>\n<li>those you left behind are in the best state you know of, and better. Your son, may God guard him, grows and prospers every</li>\n<li>day. He has turned into a grown man, a generous merchant, and one may hope he will succeed you and add to your j\u0101h.</li>\n<li>I had already sent you letters with Ab\u016b Ya\u02bfq\u016bb Y\u016bsuf b. Ma\u1e6dr\u016b\u1e25, may God keep him, in which I explained to you</li>\n<li>everything you need to know about (your) affairs, and what had reached me by way of a letter from \u1e62adaqa&rsquo;s mother or [ &hellip; ]</li>\n<li>his son Ab\u016b l-Khayr, may God keep him. I received and had someone copy out the petition and asked ...</li>\n<li>with each other, but it can be completed only in your presence, may God guard you. I hope that will be</li>\n<li>soon and that He will make it easy for you. I had written to you that you should do with whatever you still have from the</li>\n<li>cargo (al-\u1e25iml) whatever you think proper and profitable, and then set out with it. I hope you have done so.</li>\n<li>I asked you, my brother and master, to buy me a ra\u1e6dl of sharbaz\u012b (?) camphor, of the highest, finest quality; and of</li>\n<li>Indian tutty, genuine and fine, two mithq\u0101ls of the white kind, the kind that comes in shells, the shells of</li>\n<li>ostrich eggs; and also of the good, fine green kind, because I need to use it for my eyes;</li>\n<li>and of fine paper like this kind, 5,000 good sheets; and of \u1e6dal\u1e25\u012b [paper], 1,000 sheets of top quality.</li>\n<li>As for the requests my earlier letter mentioned, which I have forgotten and not listed this</li>\n<li>time, you, may God keep you, need no one to instruct you about them. As for Ab\u016b l-Sur\u016br, he had</li>\n<li>a good and lucrative journey. Someone whose word I trust told me that he is making a dinar per dinar \\\\in wheat/cloth (Goitein and Gil give different readings)//&nbsp;on this</li>\n<li>journey, since it was blessed for him, praise be to God. May God increase him in every good. My brother, I</li>\n<li>charged you with the matter of Ab\u016b Zikr\u012b b. al-Aq\u1e6da\u02bf\u012bn\u0101 (?), may God keep him: that you meet with him about what</li>\n<li>we have with him and spare (us) the trouble in this. We have not seen a letter from you about it, so do not neglect it.</li>\n<li>[ &hellip; ] in this world, it would be better for him, more decent and more upright. I have advised [ &hellip; ]</li>\n<li>[ &hellip; ] the Creator, exalted and glorified, upon him. Do not delay your letter regarding all matters whatsoever.</li>\n<li>[ &hellip; ] and inform [me] of them. I have written in haste, at the time the people are boarding the ship</li>\n<li>this very day. May God ease (the voyage) for them and decree their safety and the safety of all Israel, amen.</li>\n<li>Peace be upon you, and God&rsquo;s mercy and blessing. The boys, all of them, and your brothers [send] greetings.</li>\n<li>They are in Qayraw\u0101n; they celebrated the holiday with their families in the best of circumstances, may God keep them abundantly.</li>\n<li>From [ &hellip; ]</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
